# No unrequested fallbacks

Do not add random fallback behavior unless the user explicitly requests it in the prompt.

This includes:
- Default fallback values that hide missing or invalid data
- Silent fallback logic in `catch` blocks
- Automatic alternative code paths when the intended path fails
- Implicit retries or substitutions not asked for in the prompt

When fallback behavior might be useful, ask the user first instead of adding it by default.
